      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.colourdots.co.za/zonnebloem/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "After emancipation, Zonnebloem became a community for freed slaves, merchants, and laborers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.colourdots.co.za/zonnebloem/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1867, the area was designated the sixth municipal district of Cape Town, known as District Six.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.colourdots.co.za/zonnebloem/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "During the 1970s, apartheid laws forced non‑white residents from Zonnebloem into informal settlements outside the city.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.sa-venues.com/attractionswc/zonnebloem.php"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Today, Zonnebloem hosts the Cape Peninsula University of Technology and a few police housing units.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.sa-venues.com/attractionswc/zonnebloem.php"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Zonnebloem lies just south of the City Bowl, near galleries, boutiques, markets, and restaurants.",
